+description: "Lets a cheap model run your Kanban board and calls a stronger model only where the board or the tool results show it is needed. Mom (a good, affordable model) answers stuck signals, risky commands and completion checks; olymp (the expensive heavyweight) is asked only when mom escalates a rare high-stakes case, with hard limits per card and per day. Disclosure — once enabled, the plugin observes every kanban worker tool result (hashes and counts only, logged to logs/calling-mom.jsonl). With the advisor enabled AND a board or card opted in, redacted run excerpts go through Hermes's ctx.llm to the mom and olymp models you choose; the answer is appended to the tool result and written to the card with the public kanban_comment tool. A card line verify: <command> runs an allowlisted command (no shell, scrubbed environment) for cards created by trusted creators. hermes calling-mom setup writes the plugin's own config (calling_mom.* and its plugins.entries allowlist) with the values you pick, reads delegation.backends.model_map (read-only, to offer your Advanced Delegation routes) and creates one cron job, 'calling-mom: sweep', unless you pass --no-cron; the sweep reads the kanban databases and may push metrics to Pushgateway URLs you configure (off by default). No telemetry, no credentials stored. Since 1.4: a Desktop page (Needs you, Active cards, recent activity, status-bar chip) served by the plugin's dashboard route; it reads the log and the opted-in boards, writes only when you press a button (an answer card comment, a card move including complete, archive and unblock, written straight to the kanban database through Hermes' internal kanban module), and shows each running card's last assistant message read through Hermes' SessionDB (read-only, local, never sent to a model). web_verify (off by default) sends a one-line redacted claim to Hermes' own web_search tool. The sweep and the optional chat-wait count read board events and the human-input hooks (kinds and seconds only, never prompt or answer text). The plugin sends nothing to a server of its own; details in SECURITY.md of the repo. Since 1.7.0: what waits under Needs you is also sent once to your phone by running Hermes' own hermes send CLI (setting calling_mom.notify.target, default off), and a reply in the chat the notice went to answers the card via the tool calling_mom_answer, whose 'allow' answer releases a held command once without a further prompt from the plugin; a held critical command can be fail-closed (opt-in calling_mom.preflight.fail_closed) so it stays blocked when Mom cannot check it; a new card can be started from the Dashboard page (POST /card through Hermes' public kanban_create); a card can be parked with Decide later and resumed from the Later section. Since 1.7.1: that New card form can also pin the card's model (a model of one of your authenticated providers, sent to kanban_create as model/provider; GET /new-card lists them)."
