+name: faultline
+repo: https://github.com/bigmantech001/Faultline
+sha: "d0c2b43c2b6aa7c4fed4295a47bf9c8ad87f0616"
+version: "0.1.1"
+title: Faultline
+description: "Local API flight recorder for debugging HTTP services with Hermes. The agent starts a loopback reverse proxy in front of your service, captures every request and response (auth headers and secret JSON fields redacted before storage), learns an OpenAPI 3.1 contract from healthy traffic and flags drift (type changes, missing fields, 5xx, latency regressions), injects chaos faults (429/5xx, latency, truncated JSON), and after a fix replays the exact failing request to prove 500 -> 200. Ships six tools, a tool_execution middleware, /faultline and `hermes faultline` commands, a bundled skill, a Faultline tab in the web dashboard, and a Hermes Desktop studio page, waterfall pane, status chip and inline ::faultline-trace card. Disclosure — the proxy listens on 127.0.0.1 only and forwards to the target_url you give it (normally local; any http(s) host is accepted except literal link-local, cloud-metadata and reserved addresses and the cloud-metadata hostnames, and the URL may not carry a query, fragment or credentials); replay re-sends captured requests to the upstream they were recorded from only (the agent cannot choose another host), resolves it first and refuses link-local and cloud-metadata addresses, reaches loopback/private targets only when the owner enables the allow_local_replay setting (off by default), and replaying a POST repeats its side effects; captured traffic, contracts and chaos rules are stored in SQLite under $HERMES_HOME/plugin-data/faultline/; each running proxy is a daemon thread in the Hermes process; no telemetry, no other network calls, no credentials read, no shell commands, no Python dependencies."
+maintainer: bigmantech001
+tier: community
+category: tools
+requires_hermes: ">=0.22.5"
+docs_url: ""
+readme: true
+platforms: [linux, macos]
+screenshots:
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bigmantech001/Faultline/d0c2b43c2b6aa7c4fed4295a47bf9c8ad87f0616/docs/screenshots/dashboard-replay.png
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bigmantech001/Faultline/d0c2b43c2b6aa7c4fed4295a47bf9c8ad87f0616/docs/screenshots/dashboard-inspector.png
+  - https://raw.githubusercontent.com/bigmantech001/Faultline/d0c2b43c2b6aa7c4fed4295a47bf9c8ad87f0616/docs/screenshots/dashboard-drift.png
+capabilities:
+  provides_tools:
+    - faultline_proxy
+    - faultline_traces
+    - faultline_replay
+    - faultline_contract
+    - faultline_chaos
+    - faultline_simulate
+  provides_hooks:
+    - post_tool_call
+    - on_session_start
+  provides_middleware:
+    - tool_execution
+  requires_env: []
+known_issues:
+  - "Replay against a local service needs the owner setting allow_local_replay: true (off by default). faultline_simulate's built-in service is exempt because the plugin starts it itself."
+  - "Redacted auth headers are not replayed; pass fresh ones with faultline_replay(override_headers=...) for authenticated endpoints."
+  - "Compressed (gzip/br) response bodies are proxied untouched but stored as a placeholder, so schema drift is only learned from uncompressed JSON."
+  - "Chaos rules persist in the database and apply to every running proxy until removed."
+  - "Both halves ship opt-in: enable the agent half (hermes plugins enable faultline, then restart the gateway) and flip the Desktop switch in Capabilities -> Plugins."
diff --git a/plugin-catalog/feishu-new-topic.yaml b/plugin-catalog/feishu-new-topic.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 00000000000..d29eb8861fb
--- /dev/null
+++ b/plugin-catalog/feishu-new-topic.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+name: feishu-new-topic
+repo: https://github.com/kaigregliu/hermes-feishu-new-topic
+sha: "d8da4b34f3e0354e01f88f42ec1ddc36e74398c5"
+version: "0.3.5"
+title: Feishu New Topic
+description: "Feishu/Lark only: a message starting with `#new ` (or the spoken phrase 开启一个新话题) opens a new Feishu topic on that message, which Hermes turns into a new session — a second lane, while the session that was already running keeps running with its turn untouched. That is the difference from `/new`, which interrupts the running turn and clears the conversation. Inside a topic the trigger is stripped, because Feishu topics do not nest; if topic creation fails the message is dispatched normally with a note. Disclosure — Feishu/Lark only. Hooks `pre_gateway_dispatch` (runs before gateway auth) and checks the sender itself with the gateway's authorization probe; unauthorised senders, in-topic messages and cached duplicates cause no calls. For an authorised `#new` message it makes two Feishu OpenAPI calls through the receiving bot's own client (messages/{id}/reply with reply_in_thread, retried up to three times, then messages/{id}/delete of the one-character placeholder), sets the message's thread id so Hermes routes it to a new session, and strips the trigger from the text. Reaches gateway/adapter internals (`_is_user_authorized_for_source`, `_delivery_adapter_for`, the Feishu adapter's `_client` and `_run_blocking`), so a core refactor can stop topic creation (the message is then dispatched normally with a note). Keeps a 40-entry message-id → thread-id dedupe map in plugin state. Appended notes are Chinese-only. Requires plugins.isolation: in_process."
+maintainer: kaigregliu
+tier: community
+category: platform
+requires_hermes: ">=0.22"
+docs_url: https://github.com/kaigregliu/hermes-feishu-new-topic/blob/d8da4b34f3e0354e01f88f42ec1ddc36e74398c5/README.md
+readme: true
+capabilities:
+  provides_tools: []
+  provides_hooks: [pre_gateway_dispatch]
+  provides_middleware: []
+  requires_env: []
+known_issues:
+  - "Feishu only: the plugin is a no-op on every other platform."
+  - "Requires plugins.isolation: in_process (the default). Under host isolation the hook receives a placeholder gateway, so the plugin cannot resolve the receiving bot or the sender's authorization and does nothing."
+  - "Topics do not nest: sent inside a topic, the trigger is stripped and the message stays in the current session."
+  - "In a group, @-mentioning someone else alongside the bot makes the adapter prepend a [Mentioned: …] hint, so the trigger no longer starts the text and does not fire."
+  - "The notes the plugin appends (empty-body placeholder, in-topic note, failure notes) are Chinese-only, whatever language the user writes in."
+  - "If Feishu processes the reply but every response is lost, the plugin never learns the thread_id: the message falls back to the current session and the server-side topic can be left orphaned. Retries reuse one request UUID, which makes a duplicate topic unlikely but cannot resolve that ambiguity."
+  - "Reads gateway/adapter internals (_delivery_adapter_for, the adapter's _client and _run_blocking). They exist in Hermes 0.22 and are used by bundled plugins, but a Feishu-adapter refactor can break topic creation — the message is then dispatched normally with a note, never dropped."
