ugh 30 November 2026), whose requests Fish may use to improve its models; when no model is set and your Fish wallet shows no API credit, free credit or past top-up, the plugin uses that free model (allow_free_model: false turns this off). The key comes from the profile's secret scope (Hermes stores it in the profile .env; a single-profile install may also read FISH_API_KEY from the environment). Generated audio and subtitles are written to Hermes's audio cache; clone samples, cover images and recordings it uploads must be regular audio or image files, and Hermes config, secret and credential paths are refused. Cloning and deleting voices from chat or the model tools go through Hermes's approval gate and follow your approval settings. The Desktop Voices page and a Fish Audio settings page add gateway routes under /api/plugins/fish-audio/, behind the Hermes dashboard's existing authentication. On the Voices page, previews, clones and voice designs are billed; cloning a voice or saving a designed one creates a voice in your Fish account; cloning and deleting are confirmed on the page (a speaker-consent box, a typed voice name) instead of through Hermes's approval gate; and Use sets the profile's Fish voice, and its speech provider when none is set. The settings page, the /fish and hermes fish commands and the fish_settings tool can set or reset the profile's Fish model, voice and reading speed and save up to 50 voice names in the profile's config, so the agent can choose its own voice under the same rules; fish_pronunciations sends the pronunciation dictionary names, descriptions and rules you ask for to api.fish.audio (dictionary management is free; speech that uses a dictionary is billed as usual), can store up to three dictionary references as the profile's default in its config, and deleting a dictionary or a version goes through Hermes's approval gate; /fish setup lists what the profile still needs without a Fish call, and to tell whether a key was saved after the