+name: hermes-pentest
+repo: https://github.com/WebisityStudio/hermes-pentest
+sha: 6af5fc99bf5a8fa5303bc7b591a6a787098a5a26
+title: Hermes Pentest
+description: "Guided local Vite/Supabase source input discovery, fresh human approval, offline build and isolated testing with synthetic data. Populated/absent SQL controls and authenticated persisted-text XSS checks verify actual input/render paths. Reports distinguish rejected probes from failed controls and count planned versus completed same-user and cross-user stored workflows separately. Uses the provider already configured in Hermes. Also supports explicit local web/API discovery, controlled SQL injection, browser-proven reflected/DOM/stored XSS, access contracts, owner-approved localhost servers, multi-service applications and native/CLI checks. Durable budgets, supervised execution, stop/recovery, immutable evidence, fixed-build regression and reports. Disclosure — trusted Python controllers use the local Docker socket to manage exact run-owned containers; Docker targets get no host mounts, published ports or external network. Existing localhost servers are unmanaged and are tested only at origins the owner lists in `allowed_localhost_origins` (empty by default), which receive state-changing requests with the configured test-session headers. macOS supervised-local mode runs only executables the owner lists in `allowed_native_executables` (empty by default), under Seatbelt plus an RSS watchdog, not Docker isolation. Guided preparation reads the selected source and dependency trees and may fetch lockfile-verified Linux build packages from registry.npmjs.org. Guided assessments need a fresh one-shot human approval. Evidence stays in the selected profile's plugin data; no telemetry or model calls."
+maintainer: WebisityStudio
+tier: community
+category: tools
+version: "0.5.1"
+docs_url: https://github.com/WebisityStudio/hermes-pentest/blob/6af5fc99bf5a8fa5303bc7b591a6a787098a5a26/README.md
+platforms:
+  - linux
+  - macos
+known_issues:
+  - "Guided preparation currently supports Vite with an installed compatible npm cache and optional Supabase migrations. Other frameworks return setup gaps or require explicit adapters. Cached local toolchain images are required."
+  - "Guided execution requires Hermes public tool-execution middleware and all six declared hooks; missing approval integration refuses execution. Approval is one-use and bound to the exact source, runtime, plan and budget."
+  - "The v0.5.1 real-application follow-up completed all 15 selected checks: 10 data/Auth/browser contracts, 3 controlled SQL probes on a text preference-key filter and 2 same-user stored-XSS workflows. No confirmed vulnerabilities. Cross-user workflows: 0 planned, 0 completed. The earlier 3 rejected numeric-input SQL checks remain inconclusive; this follow-up does not relabel them or establish exhaustive coverage."
+  - "Source hints require model verification of route reachability and positive controls. Authenticated stored-XSS viewer proof requires a real final-document Bearer GET /auth/v1/user with its Referer; missing proof remains inconclusive. No arbitrary auth-state injection."
+  - "Localhost and supervised-local native targets are denied until the owner configures exact origins/executable paths in profile plugin settings. Plan acknowledgement flags do not grant permission. To revoke access, stop affected runs, end affected Hermes sessions, remove the entry, and start a new session. Managed sessions retain frozen settings; active attempts retain their bounded snapshot."
+  - "Bounded check catalogue, not exhaustive vulnerability coverage. Native support exercises CLI/app-bundle executables, not GUI/mobile interactions."
+  - "Managed web/Linux and browser checks require local Docker and prepared local images. Existing-localhost mode does not support HTTPS or interactive login/cookie rotation. Arbitrary Compose features are unsupported."
+  - "Existing localhost cannot be isolated or independently source-pinned. Interrupted unmanaged assessments require owner reset/new run. macOS native memory uses an RSS watchdog, not a hard limit."
+  - "MySQL/PostgreSQL timing has unit controls, but live dialect timing is unverified. PostgreSQL static dependency data flow is verified. SQLite and stacked MSSQL timing are explicitly skipped."
+  - "The local acceptance harness imports version-sensitive Hermes discovery internals, producing a validation warning. Plugin runtime registration/storage and secret access use public APIs."
+capabilities:
+  provides_tools:
+    - pentest_inspect
+    - pentest_prepare
+    - pentest_assess
+    - pentest_discover
+    - pentest_preflight
+    - pentest_create
+    - pentest_execute
+    - pentest_resume
+    - pentest_status
+    - pentest_stop
+    - pentest_cleanup
+    - pentest_export
+  provides_hooks:
+    - pre_tool_call
+    - pre_approval_request
+    - post_approval_response
+    - post_tool_call
+    - agent_loop_stopped
+    - on_session_end
+  provides_middleware:
+    - tool_execution
+  requires_env: []
