ermes hvault setup may unlock the key store or create the key; reads Hermes' own command line (sys.argv and sys.orig_argv, no other process's) to compare with the command bindings stored on an item by floorvault secrets allow or hermes hvault allow, and resolves a bound item only when Hermes was started with one of them (hermes hvault bind binds a new item to the command line Hermes starts its local gateway with, built from this interpreter and the profile home; --no-bind skips it) (secrets.hermesvault.require_binding, default off, also skips items with no binding); resolved values become environment variables of the Hermes process and its children, like .env entries; installs floorvault>=0.2.8,<0.5 from PyPI (plus secretstorage on Linux, pyobjc-framework-Security on macOS); one subprocess, only with custody: systemd-creds: the system's own systemd-creds (decrypt --user at startup; encrypt and decrypt in hermes hvault setup), found only in system directories, run as an argument list with no shell and a minimal environment, the key passed through a pipe; otherwise no subprocesses; no network calls, no self-update; protection is at rest, not against code already running as the same user."
