ver answers as plain text, and pins the manual with hermes curator pin; a trip export writes Trip.ics and Trip-Reference.md to a folder you choose; /pa mode writes the plugin's mode setting. A pre_tool_call hook sees every tool call and blocks only tools covered by a PA exact-action approval or its deny list, plus most tools while the ledger is unreadable; a pre_llm_call hook adds short notes to your own turns (setup offer and routing, and on a session's first turn, including another person's first turn in a shared chat, your preferences and people not yet in your files) and records which chat setup runs in. With your consent during /pa setup the agent reads USER.md, SOUL.md, its memory, the calendar, past itineraries, a context file you name and up to 20 recent sent emails (PA stores no raw mail); mail work you ask for reads messages and attachments and can write drafts (sending needs your yes); during a provider sign-in it may read your connected email or SMS for a link or code; accepted Chief of Staff jobs run scheduled turns that read PA's ledger and your USER.md or manual, may read your calendar and inbox, and search the web for your radar topics. The agent may add minimal private trip events to your calendar without asking each time, creates Kanban tasks for open commitments, and with your approval may adapt an existing brief cron job. Errands drive Hermes's browser tools on provider sites (Trip.com by default for flights and hotels, then airline or hotel sites or local sellers; reservation platforms, maps and guides for restaurants; another regional domain if blocked), in the local browser, agent-browser on Browserbase or another attended browser you configured, and provider sign-ins you give in chat are saved in the agent's credential lane and browser profile. What the agent reads and writes goes to your configured model provider as part of the conversation. Other network calls happen only when you ask or opt in: Browserbase (api.browserbase.com) with your B