+# Community catalog entry — proactive-agent
+#
+# Owner-submitted: the PR author (`JerryLiu369`) owns and maintains the repo below.
+# Exact-SHA pin (40-hex). No self-updating code, no network calls, no shell: the
+# plugin is Python hooks and one tool_execution middleware that run inside Hermes's
+# own process, plus a local SQLite ledger in the plugin's Hermes data directory.
+name: proactive-agent
+repo: https://github.com/JerryLiu369/hermes-proactive-agent
+sha: 8c6630fbb09920c83199cd73275e27d13437645a
+subdir: proactive-agent
+title: Proactive Agent
+description: "Turn governance and supervision for long chat turns. After 60 s in one turn the main agent is reminded to answer or delegate, and at 120 s editing and execution pause while reads, delegate_task and wrap-up tools stay available; a foreground terminal command running past 30 s is asked to yield to Hermes's background process registry (the same path a mid-turn user message takes) so the turn is released instead of hanging. Each subagent is briefed before it starts with the user's own words, memory and the task ledger; a subagent that returns the same step result repeatedly is stopped, a subagent's open question is carried back to the main agent, and a background subagent's result is repeated until the user has seen it. Delegated tasks are recorded in a SQLite ledger that survives gateway restarts. Governance is a positive allowlist: only the platforms named in governed_platforms (default weixin) and the subagents they spawn are affected, and every other surface runs untouched. Disclosure — registers hooks for pre_llm_call, pre_api_request, pre_auxiliary_call, post_auxiliary_call, pre_tool_call, post_tool_call, transform_tool_result, subagent_start, subagent_stop, on_session_end, on_session_reset and on_session_finalize, a system-prompt section and a tool_execution middleware, so for governed sessions it can block or amend tool calls and results, LLM request context and subagent handoffs, and asks a governed foreground terminal command still running after 30 s to move to Hermes's background process registry (through core's internal yield flag, which a Hermes release may change); it copies your Hermes USER.md and MEMORY.md memory files in full into every governed delegate_task brief, can start an internal agent turn via inject_message to re-report an unseen subagent result, and writes a local ledger.db under the plugin's Hermes data directory; no network calls, no agent tools, no credentials, no shell commands."
+maintainer: JerryLiu369
+tier: community
+category: automation
+docs_url: https://github.com/JerryLiu369/hermes-proactive-agent
+version: "0.1.16"
+requires_hermes: ">=0.22"
+capabilities:
+  provides_tools: []
+  provides_hooks:
+    - pre_llm_call
+    - pre_api_request
+    - pre_auxiliary_call
+    - post_auxiliary_call
+    - pre_tool_call
+    - post_tool_call
+    - transform_tool_result
+    - subagent_start
+    - subagent_stop
+    - on_session_end
+    - on_session_reset
+    - on_session_finalize
+  provides_middleware:
+    - tool_execution
+  requires_env: []
